    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "II — What Runs",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "Routing puts one agent in front of all the others. It reads the request, scores how confident it is, and sends it to the specialist that fits. The catch is that models are overconfident. If the router is sure and wrong, the request lands in the wrong queue and nobody notices. Set a confidence threshold, and when it is not met, ask instead of guessing.",
      "new_visual_element": "Routing — the gatekeeper and its confidence score",
