    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "II — What Runs",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "When subtasks do not depend on each other, run them at once. Split the work, hand each worker a piece, then normalize and merge what comes back. The speed-up is real — minutes become seconds. The bill is real too. Fifty concurrent calls will hit your rate limit, so you need a queue, a token bucket and backoff before you need more workers.",
      "new_visual_element": "Parallelization — split, work, normalize, merge",
